WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.868 --> 00:00:01.868
-It's kind of funny.

00:00:01.868 --> 00:00:03.868
Like, the first year
that we met,

00:00:03.868 --> 00:00:07.067
there was a really huge hit
that kind of took over

00:00:07.067 --> 00:00:11.167
our little home-school
tutorial thing.

00:00:11.167 --> 00:00:12.834
-Who is this?

00:00:12.834 --> 00:00:14.200
-Do you know -- it's called
"Idiot Boyfriend."

00:00:14.200 --> 00:00:15.234
Do you know that song?

00:00:15.234 --> 00:00:17.200
[ Laughter ]

00:00:17.200 --> 00:00:19.400
-My song?
-Yeah.

00:00:19.400 --> 00:00:20.567
-My comedy song?
-Yeah.

00:00:20.567 --> 00:00:22.033
-"Idiot Boyfriend"?

00:00:22.033 --> 00:00:25.334
-Huge hit with the --
with the Paramore crew.

00:00:25.334 --> 00:00:26.968
-I was the influence
for Paramore?

00:00:26.968 --> 00:00:28.400
-Yes!
[ Laughter ]

00:00:28.400 --> 00:00:30.334
100%.
-100%?

00:00:30.334 --> 00:00:31.567
-Yeah.
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:31.567 --> 00:00:33.400
-My disc --
[ Both laugh ]

00:00:33.400 --> 00:00:34.767
Really?
"Idiot Boyfriend"?

00:00:34.767 --> 00:00:37.234
-Thousand percent.
The music video -- iconic.

00:00:37.234 --> 00:00:39.868
-That was Zooey Desch--
-Yes!

00:00:39.868 --> 00:00:41.634
-I had a disco comedy song...
-Mm-hmm.

00:00:41.634 --> 00:00:44.400
-...when disco was at its peak.
[ Laughter ]

00:00:44.400 --> 00:00:46.334
2000 -- 2003.

00:00:46.334 --> 00:00:48.400
-Yeah.
[ Laughter ]

00:00:48.400 --> 00:00:49.934
-And --
-It was so good.

00:00:49.934 --> 00:00:51.968
-No, it was not.
-Your falsetto.

00:00:51.968 --> 00:00:55.834
-No. Where did you
even hear that song?

00:00:55.834 --> 00:00:57.601
MTV.
-MTV! Yes.

00:00:57.601 --> 00:00:58.968
-They're the only people
that would --

00:00:58.968 --> 00:01:00.901
Thank you, MTV.
They were the only people

00:01:00.901 --> 00:01:02.100
that ever played it, ever, once.

00:01:02.100 --> 00:01:04.033
-Every morning,
getting ready for, like,

00:01:04.033 --> 00:01:05.334
our home-school thing --

00:01:05.334 --> 00:01:06.734
It wasn't even, like,
really a school,

00:01:06.734 --> 00:01:09.567
but it was --
we met up to do something.

00:01:09.567 --> 00:01:12.934
And every morning had MTV on,

00:01:12.934 --> 00:01:16.000
and, like, your song
played more than, like --

00:01:16.000 --> 00:01:17.934
I think John Mayer
had a song out at the same time.

00:01:17.934 --> 00:01:19.701
[ Laughter ]

00:01:19.701 --> 00:01:21.133
-Yeah, we have
similar careers.

00:01:21.133 --> 00:01:23.200
-You got some spins, man.
You got --

00:01:23.200 --> 00:01:24.701
-I got some spins in there.

00:01:24.701 --> 00:01:26.367
Maybe we can go out
to commercial

00:01:26.367 --> 00:01:29.234
doing one of
your earliest influences.

00:01:29.234 --> 00:01:31.567
If you wouldn't mind...
[ Cheering ]

00:01:31.567 --> 00:01:34.167
...singing with me.
-I would be honored.

00:01:34.167 --> 00:01:43.734
♪♪

00:01:43.734 --> 00:01:45.767
-♪ I know what you want ♪

00:01:45.767 --> 00:01:48.033
♪♪

00:01:48.033 --> 00:01:50.133
♪ And I know what you need ♪

00:01:50.133 --> 00:01:52.801
♪♪

00:01:52.801 --> 00:01:54.834
♪ But I'm gonna screw it up ♪

00:01:54.834 --> 00:01:55.901
♪ Yeah ♪

00:01:55.901 --> 00:01:57.634
♪ 'Cause I'm an idiot ♪

00:01:57.634 --> 00:01:59.467
♪ And I'm your boyfriend ♪

00:01:59.467 --> 00:02:02.000
♪ Yes, I am ♪

00:02:02.000 --> 00:02:03.834
-♪ And I'm gon' take you out ♪

00:02:03.834 --> 00:02:06.734
♪♪

00:02:06.734 --> 00:02:08.868
♪ Leave my wallet home ♪

00:02:08.868 --> 00:02:11.300
♪♪

00:02:11.300 --> 00:02:14.467
♪ Then I'll use
your cellphone, baby ♪

00:02:14.467 --> 00:02:16.200
♪ Long distance ♪

00:02:16.200 --> 00:02:18.834
♪ 'Cause I'm your boyfriend ♪

00:02:18.834 --> 00:02:20.634
-Hayley Williams, everybody!
Come on!

